        "original_id": "0adf4b64-45e3-510f-a5b5-84b29d2735b1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: “Soleil et Chair”, “De rerum natura”\n- People: Arthur Rimbaud, Lucretius, Epicurus\n- Concepts: Atomism (social), Epicureanism\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Rimbaud’s work “Soleil et Chair” was influenced by the Roman poet and philosopher Lucretius.\n- Lucretius is jointly credited with coining the sociological theory Atomism (social).\n- Lucretius has only one known work, “De rerum natura,” which presents the tenets and philosophy of Epicureanism.\n- “De rerum natura” is about the tenets and philosophy of Epicureanism, a philosophy associated with Epicurus.",
