        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8ca1de67-3dd1-56e8-9020-b93e19d531b2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arthur Rimbaud, Horace, Virgil, Lucretius, Democritus\n- Works: Soleil et chair, De rerum natura, On the Nature of Things\n- Concepts: Romanticism, Epicureanism, atomism, social atomism, atomic theory\n- Topics: early literary style, sociological theory\n\nFacts:\n- Lucretius is a Roman philosopher associated with the ancient scientific notion of atomic theory.\n- Democritus is an ancient Greek philosopher associated with the ancient scientific notion of atomic theory.\n- Lucretius's only known work is the didactic philosophical poem De rerum natura.\n- De rerum natura presents the tenets and philosophy of Epicureanism and is usually translated into English as On the Nature of Things.\n- Social atomism, also called atomism, is a sociological theory arising from the scientific notion of atomic theory coined by Democritus and Lucretius.\n- Arthur Rimbaud's work Soleil et chair shows the influence of Romanticism and of the Latin writers Horace, Virgil, and Lucretius on his early style, while remaining unmistakably Rimbaud.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "06a0078a-9758-516f-872d-503322251b93",
        "text": "Page: Soleil et chair. Sentence: The work, while being unmistakably Rimbaud, nevertheless exhibits the influence that both Romanticism and Latin writers such as Horace, Virgil, and Lucretius had on his early style.\nPage: Lucretius. Sentence: His only known work is the didactic philosophical poem \"De rerum natura\" about the tenets and philosophy of Epicureanism, and which is usually translated into English as \"On the Nature of Things\".\nPage: Atomism (social). Sentence: Atomism or social atomism is a sociological theory arising from the scientific notion \"atomic theory\", coined by the ancient Greek philosopher Democritus and the Roman philosopher Lucretius.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
